WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Check opposition keeps Senate control blocking the Prime Minister from easy constitutional or court changes. This is Omni View, episode 209. Candidates backed by pro-Western opposition parties took 22 of the 27 seats that were up in the 81 member Czech Senate. Deutscheweller reports that Prime Minister Andre Babis' ANO movement won none of those contests and holds only 14 seats overall, a result he called unexpected. He pledged to pursue his government's agenda anyway.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.360
day, including an unpopular plan to revamp funding for public broadcasters.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.820
Check journalists have warned that this funding change could affect media independence,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.520
and the upper house's position to resist it.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.340
The two-day ballot was the first electoral test for Babis after his ANO-led coalition returned

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:53.300
to power following lower house elections in October 2025, ending a four-year break since

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.680
his first term as premier.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:00.900
That coalition, described as Eurosceptic, has already halted direct military aid to Ukraine,

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.820
and opposed European Union climate policies. Opposition parties treat the upper house majority

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:11.560
as the remaining check on those positions, because the chamber must still approve constitutional

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:17.640
amendments and constitutional court judges. Babis' own argument is that an unexpected Senate

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.920
night does not freeze the program he was returned to deliver, because the lower houses where most

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.200
ordinary laws are written. People who wanted the Senate to stay out of government

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.740
hands still grant that limit. Day-to-day bills can move without the upper chamber.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.120
Final results showed the opposition retaining the majority had already held,

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.920
after the governing coalition failed to win a single seat on the ballot.

00:01:41.051 --> 00:01:45.691
Poland's operational command of the Armed Forces said it is examining a suspected breach of

00:01:45.691 --> 00:01:51.451
national airspace overnight. Bloomberg presents that statement as a routine security alert handled

00:01:51.451 --> 00:01:56.691
by military authorities, set against ongoing regional tensions, and it does not assign

00:01:56.691 --> 00:02:02.210
the incident to any country. A major fire tore through Canadian forces' base Wainwright

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:08.050
in Alberta during a live fire training exercise on Saturday. The British Broadcasting Corporation

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:15.090
or BBC, citing the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation, or CBC, reports unnamed military sources

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:20.410
putting deaths at least at seven, while Defense Minister David McGinty described the situation

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:26.670
as active and delicate. The base is one of Canada's busiest training sites, with about 690

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:32.390
military personnel and 300 civilian workers on site on a typical day. High winds spread

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:38.150
the blaze rapidly across base fences, and Royal Alexandra Hospital and Edmonton went to a code

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:44.410
orange response. Warren Thursk, an emergency department doctor at that hospital, told the broadcaster

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.430
it is more patients than any of us want to count right now.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:53.850
He said it is a disaster, a one in every 15 to 25-year disaster, and McGinty told reporters

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.650
he cannot recall an incident like this in recent memory.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:00.670
Prime Minister Mark Carney expressed support for affected personnel.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:06.350
Alberta premier Danielle Smith called it a significant and tragic fire affecting many provincial

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:07.510
military personnel.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:13.710
Saskatchewan premier Scott Moe deployed resources to Alberta and offered more if required, and

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.810
In British Columbia, Premier David E.B. also offered assistance.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.970
The municipal district of Wainwright said the fire erupted on Saturday and tore through

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:27.190
base fences, and local authorities have urged residents to avoid the area and give emergency

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:28.550
vehicles the right of way.

00:03:29.476 --> 00:03:34.336
Families in Malaysia and neighboring countries are rushing to buy oxygen tanks and air purifiers

00:03:34.336 --> 00:03:37.416
as haze from Indonesian wildfires sits over the region.

00:03:37.956 --> 00:03:43.376
The South China Morning Post describes the months-long haze as a recurring seasonal problem that

00:03:43.376 --> 00:03:48.976
has closed schools, lifted respiratory complaints, and now pushes households toward indoor air

00:03:48.976 --> 00:03:54.516
cleaning devices. Manufacturers report a sharp rise in those purchases, and companies have

00:03:54.516 --> 00:04:00.376
been working extended shifts to meet demand. At AA alive, a medical equipment firm just outside

00:04:00.376 --> 00:04:05.756
Kuala Lumpur, employees have been working around the clock on equipment that provides clean air when

00:04:05.756 --> 00:04:11.796
outdoor conditions become hazardous. Deputy Governor Sarah Breedon of the Bank of England said certain

00:04:11.796 --> 00:04:16.016
hedge fund strategies may heighten the chance of a sudden global shock in bond markets.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:22.196
CNBC reports those remarks as a regulatory signal aimed at market participants, focused

00:04:22.196 --> 00:04:24.816
on leverage and liquidity practices in the sector.

00:04:25.356 --> 00:04:29.916
She highlighted how specific trading patterns could amplify disruptions if liquidity drives

00:04:29.916 --> 00:04:34.856
